// The live medium's Plasma desktop: upstream's panel, with the task manager's pins rewritten and
// the containment's wallpaper named. Two edits, both of which have to be made HERE rather than in
// a config file, and for the same reason — see below.
//
// LIVE MEDIUM ONLY. Stage 40 installs this (and the /etc/xdg/kdeglobals that selects the package
// carrying it) for the `installer` profile alone.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL. The Icons-Only Task Manager's stock pins come from its own
// KConfigXT default (plasma-desktop, applets/taskmanager/main.xml):
//
//     applications:systemsettings.desktop,applications:org.kde.discover.desktop,
//     preferred://filemanager,preferred://browser
//
// which on this medium is: System Settings, Discover, Dolphin, and a browser. Four pins, three of
// them wrong, and not one of them the thing this medium exists to do — and TWO of the four now
// resolve to nothing at all, because neither package is installed here: kde-plasma/discover is
// `#not-live` in config/portage/sets/desktop (an app store on a read-only stick that is thrown
// away in twenty minutes), and the browser is a Flatpak this profile does not preinstall, since
// FLATPAK_PREINSTALL="" and Firefox travels in the payload instead.
//
// That the package is gone does NOT make this script redundant. KService silently drops a
// launcher whose .desktop file it cannot resolve, so without the rewrite below the panel would
// come up with two icons on it — System Settings and Dolphin — and still not the installer.
//
// A KConfigXT default cannot be overridden by a config file: Plasma::Corona::config() opens
// plasma-org.kde.plasma.desktop-appletsrc with KConfig::SimpleConfig (libplasma, corona.cpp),
// which does NOT cascade, so an /etc/xdg copy of that file — the trick baloofilerc and
// kscreenlockerrc use — is never read. The layout script is the supported hook, and
// ShellCorona::loadDefaultLayout() takes it from the Look-and-Feel package.

// Upstream's panel, unmodified and by reference: kickoff, pager, icontasks, the system tray, the
// clock, and the input-method panel it adds only for the ~29 languages that need one. Copying
// those 70 lines here to edit one widget's config would silently freeze them at 6.6.6.
loadTemplate("org.kde.plasma.desktop.defaultPanel")

// The first change. applications:calamares.desktop is app-admin/calamares's own menu entry in
// /usr/share/applications — not our /etc/xdg/autostart copy, which is not in an applications
// directory and could not be resolved from here. Upstream's entry is also the translated one
// ("Instalar el sistema", "システムをインストール", …), which matters on a medium whose first
// control is a language picker.
var pinned = 0;
var allPanels = panels();
for (var i = 0; i < allPanels.length; i++) {
    var tasks = allPanels[i].widgets("org.kde.plasma.icontasks");
    for (var t = 0; t < tasks.length; t++) {
        tasks[t].currentConfigGroup = ["General"];
        tasks[t].writeConfig("launchers", ["applications:calamares.desktop"]);
        tasks[t].reloadConfig();
        pinned++;
    }
}
// Not fatal: a panel is far better than no panel, and the medium is still usable with the stock
// pins. Said out loud so it is one grep in the live session's journal rather than a mystery.
if (pinned === 0) {
    print("installer layout: no org.kde.plasma.icontasks widget was found in the default panel; " +
          "the task manager kept its stock launchers");
}

// The second change, and it is not cosmetic here — it is what keeps the desktop from coming up
// black. Breeze's layout sets 'org.kde.image' and leaves the image itself to
// org.kde.breeze.desktop/contents/defaults:
//
//     [Wallpaper]
//     Image=Next
//
// `Next` is not on this medium. kde-plasma/plasma-workspace-wallpapers is dropped from the set on
// a live profile (`#not-live` in config/portage/sets/desktop, 216.8 MiB) and stage 50 section 3i
// deletes the 38.3 MiB Breeze ships as `Next`, which cannot be dropped as a package because
// breeze is also the widget style, the colour scheme and the look-and-feel fallback. Left alone,
// org.kde.image resolves `Next` to nothing and draws an empty containment — plasma-workspace's
// DefaultWallpaper::defaultWallpaperPackage() falls back from the look-and-feel `defaults` to the
// Plasma theme and then to `wallpapers/Next` again, so every arm of that fallback is missing too.
//
// So the plugin stays org.kde.image and the image is NAMED here: one wallpaper package, this
// distro's own, installed by stage 40 for this profile only from config/calamares/system/
// wallpaper and left alone by section 3i when it deletes everything else under
// /usr/share/wallpapers. It is 0.4 MiB against the collection's 255.1, so the medium keeps a
// branded desktop and still gives back 254.7 MiB of the artwork it used to carry.
//
// AN ABSOLUTE PATH, not the package's id, and that is a constraint rather than a style choice:
// MediaProxy::setSource() puts this value through QUrl::fromUserInput(), which turns a bare
// "@DISTRO_ID@" into an http:// URL and not into a wallpaper. A directory is what the wallpaper
// KCM itself stores, and determineProviderType() reads Provider::Type::Package straight off it
// being one.
//
// FillMode is deliberately NOT written. Its KConfigXT default is 2, PreserveAspectCrop, which is
// what a 2.40:1 image has to have on a 16:9 or 4:3 panel; the mark sits right of centre and
// survives the crop at both. Writing the default would only freeze it.
//
// The lock screen is a different config file and is covered separately, in
// config/calamares/system/kscreenlockerrc.in: kscreenlocker's greeter reads its own
// [Greeter][Wallpaper][org.kde.image][General], never this containment's.
var desktopsArray = desktopsForActivity(currentActivity());
for (var d = 0; d < desktopsArray.length; d++) {
    desktopsArray[d].wallpaperPlugin = 'org.kde.image';
    desktopsArray[d].currentConfigGroup = ['Wallpaper', 'org.kde.image', 'General'];
    desktopsArray[d].writeConfig('Image', '/usr/share/wallpapers/@DISTRO_ID@/');
}
